{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons","id":171852,"title":"Lesser Elemental Dragons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-17T12:22:04-07:00","id":171852,"title":"Lesser Elemental Dragons","content":"While not my favorite Elementals, I find these guys interesting. Elementals in general are sort of the &quot;second class citizen&quot; of the spirit world, and yet these are about the only guys powerful and sophisticated enough that even Gods must respect them. It would be fascinating to see how different ED deal with this; some employ only other Elementals, treating them well, while others lord it over them, probably while currying the favor of &quot;elite&quot; Gods; while others may employ only minor Gods, and treat them like crap. <br /> <br /> We know how Lesser ED can become Greater ones, but I don't think the books ever say how a LED comes about. Can a massive dragon line disturbance give rise to an ED from scratch? Or is ever LED previously another type of Elemental that somehow raised its Essence until it became what it is, at Ess 7? Interestingly, the LED created by Sidereal Charms start at Ess 4, and are clearly the weakest of their kind, at least until they can raise their understanding of their new spiritual state somehow. It would be cool to follow the story of one of those and how he made his way in the world and gained acceptance of his new kind (or didn't)!<br /> <br /> I'm sure the books don't say, but roughly how many LED do you imagine exist? And what percentage of them are employed by Heaven to act as Censors, or work for some Bureau or other? <br /> <br /> The ones that don't have jobs are intriguing, too. I imagine many of them hide their light under a bushel, traveling shapeshifted as some form of harmless human, interacting with people, and pursuing their hobbies. Only occasionally are they moved to drop their guise or reveal their powers, and many local legends grow from these events...<br /> <br /> Of course, Exalted will often be at the center of these legends. If a ST gets tired of fellow Exalted NPCs as teachers, and esp wants a mythic tone, he could do much worse than having PCs seek out or stumble across an ED, either living in plain sight as part of a human community or in its &quot;natural&quot; form, out in the wilderness somewhere. They make for great mentors and sifus, being able to practice and teach up to the Celestial level of sorcery and martial arts, as well as being storehouses of forgotten lore and able to forge great weapons. <br /> <br /> This all makes them pretty damn powerful, as well. Frankly, they are probably the most powerful being walking creation in mass numbers, outside of the Exalted themselves. I'd say they're pretty much direct matches for Second Circle Demons, all things being even (which they rarely are, of course!). This is why I think there probably aren't that many of them, relatively speaking. And they're hardly invincible, esp not with various forms of Spirit Slaying charms around! Avenging one's fallen (or enslaved) LED master/friend could be a cool plot hook...<br /> <br /> What are some cool visuals for Dragons you've thought of? I have this image in my head of an eastern dragon made of various precious woods, all polished to a high glossy shine...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:34:17-07:00","id":171953,"title":"","content":"So here's something I thought of making a post about yesterday, but my keyboard is shot.<br /> <br /> Lesser elemental dragons weren't actually elementals until 2e, as far as I can gather.<br /> <br /> In the 1e corebook, their nature is kind of vague (as in not talked about at all) and Fakhuru was the sample <i>god</i>, had Materialize and wasn't stated at all as to being an elemental. The part of the &quot;Antagonists&quot; chapter on elementals said that they can become draconic with more Essence, but never says they become dragons. Nothing is said on this with the <i>Exalted Storyteller's Companion</i> either.<br /> <br /> The next book to talk about elementals in depth was <i>Games of Divinity</i>. The Five Elemental Dragons are implied as to being gods (the last of the great ones or something) and are often referred to with the groupings of &quot;...sun, moon, stars, and the turning of the seasons.&quot; The section on elementals makes it pretty clear that the original elementals were different beings from the Five Elemental Dragons. It also never says that the new sorts of elementals become elemental dragons. Instead, it calls lesser elemental dragons the children of the Five Elemental Dragons. And while the dragons are listed as Godlike Elemental Beings, it never in the write-ups for the elemental dragons (Swan Dragon and scuh) actually calls them elementals. Confusing things still, the dragons have costs to Materialize, indicating they're some other sort of spirit.<br /> <br /> <i>Exalted: the Sidereals</i> doesn't do much to clarify this. It calls the lesser elemental dragons divinities (gods). Again, they have Materialize.<br /> <br /> Some dragons first introduced in 1e confuse this further though. There's the Frog Queen, First Wood Spider (<i>Savant &amp; Sorcerer</i>), and the Wind Masters being more or less like souped-up versions of existing elementals. The relationship between dragons and elementals like them is made even less clear.<br /> <br /> Dragons that are straight-up big elementals don't happen until <i>Exalted: the Auchthonians</i>, where the sample crystal elemental is a lesser elemental dragon of crystal and has Dematerialize. This isn't utilized again until the 2e corebook, which reigns elemental dragons into being high Essence elementals, probably in light of the decision to overlly make the 5ED Gaia's souls.<br /> <br /> With the Five Elemental Dragons no longer overtly being this, as well as a bit of a discharging of 2e's decisions on setting metaphysics, I kind of wonder what that means for how lesser and greater elemental dragons might be like.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:49:09-07:00","id":171984,"title":"","content":"Hm, interesting notes, thanks, Blaque!<br /> <br /> 2E did a lot to classify things that were vague before, sometimes for the better, sometimes for the worse. YMMV on which is which, of course. For my part, I like what it did and hope that they remain Elementals more or less as 2E defined them, which works pretty well for them and the setting as a whole. <br /> <br /> Any thoughts on the other points I brought up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T13:51:44-07:00","id":171985,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer the interpretation of the 5ED being Gaia's souls. it means that the dragon blooded actually did get a portion of her power like they are supposed to have instead of it being delegated to five lesser entities who should have had no trouble crafting standard exaltations and thus rendering the entire defining feature of dragon blooded pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T14:12:06-07:00","id":172013,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much on board with everything you said about LED. I think they should play a fairly active role within the Terrestrial Hierarchy. And I also applaud having them travel around creation shapeshifted into mortal form of some kind (sometimes human, sometimes animal or plant life etc) in order to get a sense of whats happening in the world or in some cases, to socialize with beings of a more philosophical nature than the elementals they usually deal with. An LED would make an excellent patron for an Exalted Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T15:54:45-07:00","id":172109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=171985#post171985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it means that the dragon blooded actually did get a portion of her power like they are supposed to have</div> </div> </div> </div>They're supposed to what now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">instead of it being delegated to five lesser entities who should have had no trouble crafting standard exaltations and thus rendering the entire defining feature of dragon blooded pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soooo what, the Dragon Blooded being a kind of inferior knock off of proper Exalted is bad when they come from the Elemental Dragons, but all right when they come from Gaia?<br /> <br /> One still begs the question of what a &quot;standard Exaltation&quot; is and why anybody should be worried about being it.<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial Exalted are what they are because they could be nothing else. Same as the Alchemical Exalted; the Maker being a Primordial doesn't entitle them to greater or different power, and there's not some Solar-sized Exalted he's keeping in reserve against the time where he's not so cowardly as to fear relying on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T16:12:48-07:00","id":172123,"title":"","content":"[Books of Sorcery Vol. IV, pg. 73] <br /> &quot;<i>With Gaia\u2019s tutelage, and the aid of the Elemental Dragons, the Incarnae learned the secrets of creating life unlike themselves. With this secret in their grasp, they began work on a race of five great beings &lt;elementals&gt; who would regulate the natural processes of Creation\u2019s elements.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> [Books of Sorcery Vol. IV, pg. 94, 125] <br /> Doldrum evolves into Serefu and Heketa evolves into Frog Queen. The evolutionary line is unique to each elemental, I hope so.<br /> <br /> [Books of Sorcery Vol. IV, pg. 79-80]<br /> They have Limit Break of months. <br /> <br /> [John Morke]<br /> <i>Elementals are simpler than gods, and in some instances more powerful. They don't expand their purview to become more complex and thereby gain more complex magic, but they don't rely on portfolios, either.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the changes of 1st ed. to 2nd ed. will be established in the 3rd ed. Gradually they gain feature to be player characters - unlike the gods. Would play with them. In the same manner opened to play with Raksha. So I thought of a way to use slavery: elementals could have levels pact as ghosts have Passion. Thus recover willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T03:08:17-07:00","id":172582,"title":"","content":"Roles I've used LED's in include:<br /> <br /> The movers and shakers in terrestrial courts both benign and corrupt. Ive had them as allies for my players and occasionally minor antogonists never an outright opponenet. I had one story where my players got caught in the middle of a cenutries old conflict between two memebers of a spirit court who were both L.E.Ds<br /> <br /> I have had a Wood spider who harnessed a personal cult from several settlements evolve into a LED during the course of one of my story lines. He was an interesting character part informant, part manipulator. He was pretty cruel to his cult, manipulating them at his own whim for pleasure in their conflict but my players didnt have much of an issue with this. He kind of faded out of the story but I would definintely like to reinitroduce him into other stories, maybe where he is attempting to attain a heavenly position or dominance of a loval spirit court.<br /> <br /> Ive never done the unstable LED seeking to elevate himslef to a GED but could see how this story could be cool.<br /> <br /> I have used LEDs in their capacity as Celestial Censor in a Sidereal game I ran. It was a LED of Earth replete with gemstone bling and was really comic relief. He didnt really like the circle but my players loved to wind him up whilst aiding his investigations and he was a fun character in anotherwise quite Noir story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T03:09:39-07:00","id":172583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172109#post172109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Terrestrial Exalted are what they are because they could be nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the reason they could be nothing else was that primordial essence was used in their creation, which is stated to be too powerful to be encapsulated in the same manner that the gods' was. You'll notice that alchemicals and terrestrials share a common theme of being slightly less powerful and not having a set number being in existence. And that this is achieved in a manner appropriate to their patron. And if the Elemental Dragons are independent entities on the same level as the incarna then why would they need to bother messing with the formula? Being a primordial doesn't entitle one to different power, it <i>neccesitates it. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T03:57:22-07:00","id":172614,"title":"","content":"Thing is the 5ED aren't Incarnae. Going by what the devs have said, they are the children of Gaia, unique unto themselves.<br /> <br /> As such, they're not going to Exalt as the Incarnae do. They're going to do it in a way that resonates with their nature, a way that speaks of heritage and the elements.<br /> <br /> I mean, that justification was off the top of my head. The 5EDs' method of Exaltation doesn't have to have anything to do with Gaia's nature, 'cause it's about, you know, the 5EDs.<br /> <br /> And the devs don't have to abide by previous depictions of how Dragon-Blooded Exaltation came about; arguing _based_ on those previous depictions, when those depictions can be overwritten, means you're arguing based on something that isn't likely to apply anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T04:23:51-07:00","id":172621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and the reason they could be nothing else was that primordial essence was used in their creation, which is stated to be too powerful to be encapsulated in the same manner that the gods' was. You'll notice that alchemicals and terrestrials share a common theme of being slightly less powerful and not having a set number being in existence. And that this is achieved in a manner appropriate to their patron. And if the Elemental Dragons are independent entities on the same level as the incarna then why would they need to bother messing with the formula? Being a primordial doesn't entitle one to different power, it neccesitates it.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Dragon Blooded were served so much better when they weren't surrounded by a bizarre sense of unease at their difference from Celestial Exalted that drove people to create stupid elaborate explanations for it. It's an assumption that should be changed all on its own; hopefully, new Exalted will help to serve the transition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T04:47:08-07:00","id":172629,"title":"","content":"I think that's a completely reasonable question given that their prototype (Jade Caste Alchemicals) don't differ from the others in any significant way. There had to be some reason for the drastic change and the 5ED being &quot;unique&quot; doesn't really cut it because <i>all </i>the incarna are unique. The Maidens just randomly popped up out of nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T05:04:20-07:00","id":172643,"title":"","content":"True enough. Why, I remember when I reread the First Edition core and Exalted: the Dragon Blooded, and took note of that little mention of the Jade Caste Alchemicals being the prototypes of the Terrestrial Exalted and thought to myself &quot;but wait, that Caste isn't as different from the others as the Terrestrials are from the Celestials&quot;, and I turned to Holden to ask him why this should be. Then he removed his laser mask to reveal Ron Perlman, at which point the Major came in to say how silly everything had become, and I woke up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T05:29:47-07:00","id":172654,"title":"","content":"I like coming up with this stuff anyway. Gaia's soul hierarchy is left so vague there's plenty of room to speculate and I just find the notion of the 5ED being her souls just seems neater than coming up with this other explanation involving unique existences and children and all that. It doesn't really add anything to the narrative, IMHO. Aren't a primordial's souls sometimes referred to in a familial sense anyway? <br /> <br /> One of my pet theories is that elementals are a weird sort of first circle deva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T05:35:11-07:00","id":172664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172654#post172654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't a primordial's souls sometimes referred to in a familial sense anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really - not enough for your forced compartmentalization to really work here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T06:12:18-07:00","id":172698,"title":"","content":"I have not got a grip or an opinion about the Elemental Dragons. I have seen references here and there, as in the 2ed Core book. But I never managed to find anything tangible, or otherwise useful.<br /> <br /> But this thread have given me a lot of food for thoughts. I mean, comparing them to demons makes perfect sense to me. After all, why would the ability to &quot;subdivide&quot; the soul into different entities be something the Primordials learned after they got defeated? So why elementals? Instead of looking at the world as built by elements, turning it around; after all Gaia is generally &quot;the soul of the world&quot;. I mean, they made a prison out of Malfeas; where did they got that idea? Because perhaps there was a precedence, Gaia as creation? That would also put the Luna/Gaia romance in another light.<br /> <br /> I would have to toss out the &quot;Gaia left creation and is out exploring somewhere else&quot; bit. But I don't have any problems with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T06:17:10-07:00","id":172699,"title":"","content":"What can I say. I'm a Lumper.<br /> <br /> I just don't really see the point of making these guys a distinct class of being all of their own when there's a vacant spot in the metaphysics in which they fit perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T07:14:26-07:00","id":172775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172699#post172699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can I say. I'm a Lumper.<br /> <br /> I just don't really see the point of making these guys a distinct class of being all of their own when there's a vacant spot in the metaphysics in which they fit perfectly fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a thoroughly explained, perfectly internally consistent cosmology that can be accurately represented on a graph makes everything more predictable and takes away from Creation as the savage and exotic world of myth.<br /> <br /> ...I just realized how bizarre it is that Alchemicals, first introduced to the game in order to upset the metaphysical status quo and demonstrate that anything can happen in Creation, are now considered essential to creating a coherent cosmological theory about the nature of the Exaltations.<br /> <br /> \u200bSeriously, the only reason Alchemical Castes are described the way they are is to make them feel like bizarro-Exalted from another dimension, in line with the then-standard plot hook of &quot;communist robots from outer space attack&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T07:34:57-07:00","id":172790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172698#post172698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this thread have given me a lot of food for thoughts. I mean, comparing them to demons makes perfect sense to me. After all, why would the ability to &quot;subdivide&quot; the soul into different entities be something the Primordials learned after they got defeated? So why elementals? Instead of looking at the world as built by elements, turning it around; after all Gaia is generally &quot;the soul of the world&quot;. I mean, they made a prison out of Malfeas; where did they got that idea? Because perhaps there was a precedence, Gaia as creation? That would also put the Luna/Gaia romance in another light.<br /> <br /> I would have to toss out the &quot;Gaia left creation and is out exploring somewhere else&quot; bit. But I don't have any problems with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia = Creation was an idea that people latched onto in First Edition and was the default interpretation for most of Second Edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T07:47:17-07:00","id":172795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172775#post172775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a thoroughly explained, perfectly internally consistent cosmology that can be accurately represented on a graph makes everything more predictable and takes away from Creation as the savage and exotic world of myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mother Nature has dragons for souls. How much more savage and exotic can you get?<br /> <br /> Also I thoroughly subscribe to the &quot;understanding how stuff works just makes it cooler&quot; school of thought. A mystery is only interesting if it has an answer to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-18-2014, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T08:08:20-07:00","id":172809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172790#post172790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia = Creation was an idea that people latched onto in First Edition and was the default interpretation for most of Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Being a bit late to the party tend to make me quite unaware of what people has discussed before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T08:47:18-07:00","id":172840,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Lesser Elemental Dragons were really just grown-up Elementals: what naturally happens when an elemental reaches Essence 6-7. Honestly, I never worried about it that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:34:55-07:00","id":172902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172795#post172795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I thoroughly subscribe to the &quot;understanding how stuff works just makes it cooler&quot; school of thought. A mystery is only interesting if it has an answer to find.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, I can't think of one mystery WW answered in any of their games that didn't disappoint me on some level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:40:42-07:00","id":172919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172664#post172664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really - not enough for your forced compartmentalization to really work here.</div> </div> </div> </div>What &quot;forced compartmentalization&quot;? That <i>was the default definition of them for most of 2E, and no one had a problem with it,</i> until 3E said &quot;we're going with something else&quot;. Sometimes I think we forget that this is all just made-up stuff, and it stands or falls on the writers' ability to sell us on a plausible explanation. The Five Elemental Dragons being 5 of Gaia's souls wasn't the original explanation, but it made at least as much sense, if not more. It works just fine. Now, we're getting still another definition of them, and *that* should work just fine, too. <br /> <br /> We don't need the &quot;Edition Wars&quot; nonsense of dumping on previous works just to justify liking the new stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:44:03-07:00","id":172921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermes12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172582#post172582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roles I've used LED's in include:<br /> <br /> The movers and shakers in terrestrial courts both benign and corrupt. Ive had them as allies for my players and occasionally minor antogonists never an outright opponenet. I had one story where my players got caught in the middle of a cenutries old conflict between two memebers of a spirit court who were both L.E.Ds<br /> <br /> I have had a Wood spider who harnessed a personal cult from several settlements evolve into a LED during the course of one of my story lines. He was an interesting character part informant, part manipulator. He was pretty cruel to his cult, manipulating them at his own whim for pleasure in their conflict but my players didnt have much of an issue with this. He kind of faded out of the story but I would definintely like to reinitroduce him into other stories, maybe where he is attempting to attain a heavenly position or dominance of a loval spirit court.<br /> <br /> Ive never done the unstable LED seeking to elevate himslef to a GED but could see how this story could be cool.<br /> <br /> I have used LEDs in their capacity as Celestial Censor in a Sidereal game I ran. It was a LED of Earth replete with gemstone bling and was really comic relief. He didnt really like the circle but my players loved to wind him up whilst aiding his investigations and he was a fun character in anotherwise quite Noir story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are some cool stories and give me some neat ideas! Your Earth Dragon in particular...I'm imagining a Gem Lord who gets a power boost due to some geomantic engineering, and his gems form into his new, draconic body, bursting up from the ground! He never knew what it was to be able to freely move around before, what does he do now? <br /> <br /> Of course, if this is on the Blessed Isle, where I think there should be lots of Gem Lords, then the nearby Immaculates will want a word with him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T15:42:49-07:00","id":173270,"title":"","content":"Maybe I wouldn't object to the Elemental Dragons as souls of Gaia if that wasn't a thing that was extrapolated into so much &quot;Terrestrials are larval Gaia Exalted&quot; horseshit. But it was, and that kind of taints the whole concept, so there you go. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't really see the point of making these guys a distinct class of being all of their own when there's a vacant spot in the metaphysics in which they fit perfectly fine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good luck with the dark mother and whatever's behind the Getimians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T16:00:46-07:00","id":173287,"title":"","content":"Is there something the dark mother would blatantly fit as being while everyone seems to deny that she is and makes out she's this super special awesome unique thing another being pulled out of it's ass in a totally unorthodox way for no apparent reason? And then did the same again with another set of beings which serve roughly the same purpose assuming that the role the first set blatantly fit in is not the one they actually fill? If so i think I will be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T16:55:39-07:00","id":173339,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing on dragons in 2e. That was more or less something becoming canon and defining something which had been previously left open. And actually contradicted some of what had been there before.<br /> <br /> In <i>Games of Divinity</i>, the Five Elemental Dragons were gods. And they made Dragon-Blooded the way they did not becuase of some connection to Gaia, but because they were simply weaker than the Incarna and Terrestrial Exaltation manifested the way it did as a consequence of their nature. Other beings in 3e will do this it looks like, such as the case with Exigents and other new Exalted.<br /> <br /> The 5ED being Gaia's souls caused actual weirdness as well. As noted already, it made Gaia a huge part of the Dragon-Blooded Exaltation more than was probably intended. It more or less caused a weird retcon as to what dragons were in 2e. Until indications of Gnosis havining more, or the Twenty Hidden Souls of Gaia in Dreams, we also had this bit of the general habit of fans and authors to jump to the idea that Talked About = All that there is, making Gaia violate rules given on other Primordials (five souls innstead of at least twelve), and wasn't consistet anyhow (five souls being dragons instaed of the wide vareity of other Primordial souls, no indication of Second or First Circle Deva). It also made Gaia the important part of the Dragon-Blooded lore, rather than the indication I got out of 1e that the &quot;turning of the seasons&quot; and motherfucking dragons were supposed to be their mainn source of metaphysical weight.<br /> <br /> It more or less does to the Five Elemental Dragons like the Yozis did to their Third Circle Demons: Made them a footnote in the &quot;important&quot; entity. It made them in effect &quot;mere&quot; deva working at her whim, rather than gods with their own motivations and lore to draw on. It closed doors instead of opened them.<br /> <br /> It's also blatent retcon in the end. It wasn't the case before for that being their nature beyond fanon. And the nature of lesser and greater dragons as a result is even moreso as it outright contradicts what was before. It is just as much to decouple dragons from the elementals and Gaia again, sure. But that &quot;This is how it is now&quot; isn't a justification, and &quot;It makes the setting more concise and consistent on what beings are&quot; isn't viewed as a plus by the writers.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T17:17:06-07:00","id":173365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172614#post172614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such, they're not going to Exalt as the Incarnae do. They're going to do it in a way that resonates with their nature, a way that speaks of heritage and the elements.<br /> <br /> I mean, that justification was off the top of my head. The 5EDs' method of Exaltation doesn't have to have anything to do with Gaia's nature, 'cause it's about, you know, the 5EDs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. For the same reason, any other entity creating Exalted -- including a god granted access to the Divine Exigency -- may find the method of Exaltation little resembles that of the Incarnae, or even any other known entity, but that method will resonate with the entity's nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=172795#post172795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I thoroughly subscribe to the &quot;understanding how stuff works just makes it cooler&quot; school of thought. A mystery is only interesting if it has an answer to find.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mystery the game introduces can have an answer whether the game nails down what it is or not. The game providing an answer to a mystery gives one answer (and, well, also no mystery), the game providing no answer frees many tables to reach many answers. A complaint many have of 2e is that it answered too many of these, made the game feel too solved, and essentially allowed everything to be compartmentalized as you've been doing. I know I can find fun with this, too, but EX3 looks like it's hewing more toward not overexplaining everything, and I'm looking forward to that. For instance, I don't think EX3 will reveal -- whether overtly or in clues -- that the Scarlet Empress is in Malfeas. It's more likely to say nothing at all of what became of her.<br /> <br /> What I expect to happen is that the game will say the Five Elemental Dragons are Gaea's children, and then not say much else of their origins. It will instead spend its wordcount on things about them more relevant to their place in the world and how their natures reflect their Chosen. The game will then go onto other topics.<br /> <br /> If a table is very attached to the idea that the Dragons are Gaea's souls, their table can go nuts with that; the relatively sparse description the Dragons are likely to receive will mean that interpretation causes very little (if anything) to break. Honestly, it was canon for 2e, so lots of tables are just going to default to it. Tables who want to do something else should feel as free as possible to do so. These groups will already be fighting against the inertia of a previous edition in which the Dragons' nature was set; there's really nothing to gain in adding to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T18:51:00-07:00","id":173467,"title":"","content":"Suppose the Five Elemental Dragons are gods again, and rather than sleeping under their respective poles, they play the Games of Divinity in the Jade Pleasure Dome with the Celestial Incarnae.<br /> <br /> When one of the Maiden's win a round, the sky of Yu-Shan becomes starry night with the maiden's planet/star being most prominent. What happens when one of the Dragons wins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:21:44-07:00","id":173498,"title":"","content":"They were gods, but never were said to be in the Jade Pleasure Dome. As I gather they kind of are dicking about being absentee heads of the Terrestrial Bureacracy and had been for a while.<br /> <br /> As to what happens, my guess is weather like snow, thunderstorms, heat, or the lot. <br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T21:02:41-07:00","id":173635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173467#post173467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when one of the Dragons wins?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heaven catches fire. This is regardless of which Dragon pulls ahead. <i>That</i> is why they slumber at the Poles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T21:30:02-07:00","id":173668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173635#post173635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heaven catches fire. This is regardless of which Dragon pulls ahead. <i>That</i> is why they slumber at the Poles.</div> </div> </div> </div>So <i>that's</i> what Fire Has Wrought. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From the mentions Blaque and others made about some of the Dragons' originally emphasized associations... As the seasons turn on a different cycle than than the day-night cycle of the Incarnae, so might the dragons also run on a somewhat parallel track. Perhaps the first of the five to fulfill a separate (noticeably longer) victory condition determines the general seasonal &quot;special effects&quot; in Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T21:32:40-07:00","id":173670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173668#post173668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So <i>that's</i> what Fire Has Wrought. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From the mentions Blaque and others made about some of the Dragons' originally emphasized associations... As the seasons turn on a different cycle than than the day-night cycle of the Incarnae, so might the dragons also run on a somewhat parallel track. Perhaps the first of the five to fulfill a separate (noticeably longer) victory condition determines the general seasonal &quot;special effects&quot; in Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be kind of neat actually.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T22:29:20-07:00","id":173731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173467#post173467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose the Five Elemental Dragons are gods again, and rather than sleeping under their respective poles, they play the Games of Divinity in the Jade Pleasure Dome with the Celestial Incarnae.<br /> <br /> When one of the Maiden's win a round, the sky of Yu-Shan becomes starry night with the maiden's planet/star being most prominent. What happens when one of the Dragons wins?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather they either be Deva or their own thing, -maybe- something more connected to Elementals. I also think it would be cooler for them to remain at the poles, as it gives them a slight bit more flavour distinct from the Incarnae. Besides, their Chosen are the -Terrestrial- Exalted, which kind of necessitates a connection to the physical world.<br /> <br /> Also, because it has to be associated with the Sky; when Dana'ad wins a round it starts raining, when Mela wins it starts an electric storm, when Hesiesh wins there is a genuine firestorm, when Pasiap wins it -literally- starts raining solid rock all Malfeas like-...<br /> I would suppose that means Sextus Jylis causes trees to fall out of the sky or something dumb like that, I dunno.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T23:53:32-07:00","id":173776,"title":"","content":"The Five Elemental Dragons are the children of Gaia, like the Incarnae are the children of Primordials. Gaia created them for a purpose and that was to serve as the anchors for Creation. They are not her souls, her souls are of and on Gnosis, beyond her jouten who remains in Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> Greater and Lesser Elemental Dragons are elementals who adopt the forms of dragons in respect and reverence of the Five. They are remnants of 5 great beings made by the Incarnae with the aid of Gaia and her children to tend Creation's elements. They were struck down, and scattered. Elementals of today are remnants and shards of that power. Like many spiritual beings, their forms are ultimately mutable. Some of their number are promoted to godhood, and given responsibilities of gods.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded Exaltation is indeed fueled by the power of the Five Elemental Dragons, as the Solar Exaltation is fueled by the Unconquered Sun. Informed by their nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T00:18:09-07:00","id":173794,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the dragon blooded being weaker because the dragons are weaker that the incarnae <i>doesn't work </i>because of how many dragonblooded there are. One dragon blooded takes less power to create than a solar, sure, but initially each dragon exalted just under 7 of them for every solar Conky did, and on top of that they're self-replicating. There has been points where the dragon blooded have been said to have numbered several <i>million</i> and assuming &quot;several&quot; means three just to make the maths easier that means that there has been a point where for every solar there were approximately two thousand dragonblooded <i>of each aspect. </i>Where is all this power coming from? <br /> <br /> That's why I think they need a primordial patron. I don't think anything less could take the strain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T00:27:15-07:00","id":173798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173794#post173794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the dragon blooded being weaker because the dragons are weaker that the incarnae <i>doesn't work </i>because of how many dragonblooded there are. One dragon blooded takes less power to create than a solar, sure, but initially each dragon exalted just under 7 of them for every solar Conky did, and on top of that they're self-replicating. There has been points where the dragon blooded have been said to have numbered several <i>million</i> and assuming &quot;several&quot; means three just to make the maths easier that means that there has been a point where for every solar there were approximately two thousand dragonblooded <i>of each aspect. </i>Where is all this power coming from?<br /> <br /> That's why I think they need a primordial patron. I don't think anything less could take the strain.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand. The nature of the Terrestrial Exaltation is tied to blood, to natural Creation. This is how it is informed by their nature. They are anchors, also tied to Creation. They have been part of it's natural form since conception, and without them it would perish. They are silent, but as honored as the Incarnae.<br /> <br /> Also, you assumptions claim that Exaltations drain from the Creator, this is only true of Exigence, not Exaltations. You also assume that power cannot create more power. There is not a finite resource of Dragonblooded Exaltations. Like the natural world, they planted their power like seeds in mortals, and let nature take it's course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T00:53:49-07:00","id":173805,"title":"","content":"I will admit that I occasionally forget that conservation of energy isn't a thing where essence is concerned, but honestly I still don't really care.<br /> <br /> Ok, they're her children. woot. What does that even mean? What purpose does this distinction serve? I mean, if you killed one that would damage creation, and in some ways Gaia is supposed to be or represent creation (because otherwise why is she even called Gaia?) and so effectively they'll act as if they were her souls even if they're not. And Gaia has this big empty shelf where all her pantheon are supposed to go and I'm stood here watching everyone insist the 5ED go on their own fancy little table and I'm like &quot;for Christ's sake guys, they look fine on the shelf. Just put them there.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T01:14:55-07:00","id":173815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173798#post173798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you assumptions claim that Exaltations drain from the Creator, this is only true of Exigence, not Exaltations. You also assume that power cannot create more power. There is not a finite resource of Dragonblooded Exaltations. Like the natural world, they planted their power like seeds in mortals, and let nature take it's course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exaltation -does- drain from it's Creator, as far as Third Edition is concerned. Exigence or no. It's the Law of Diminishment; when the Sun first made the Solar Exalted, he set for the first time. When Ten Sheaves used Exigence to Exalt Janest, he had to give up his life.<br /> How exactly this relates the the Elemental Dragons and their Chosen is uncertain, but I'd go ahead and suppose that it was the creation of the original bloodlines that Diminished the Dragons, rather than the Exaltation of individual Terrestrials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T02:10:15-07:00","id":173848,"title":"","content":"Referring to Gaia's 3rd circle parts as children instead of demons sounds like a good propaganda trick. &quot;Look. The Yozis are evil things. Gaia is nothing like them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I actually like the idea of having &quot;what is&quot; and &quot;what is told&quot; separated. Especially if I can get a bunch of players that does know to much about Exalted, and trust me enough for a &quot;bait and switch campaign&quot; (as presenting the Immaculate belief as facts to the players on how the setting works).<br /> <br /> So there is a reference somewhere to Yozis having twelve 3rd circle parts? Well. Gaia isn't one of the defeated Primordials so she never had to swear the oats the Yosis had to swear. So having five parts as the Elemental Dragons, one &quot;jouten&quot; in Yu-Shan, and perhaps a couple more? Sounds like it would fit my view of it.<br /> <br /> The ED being &quot;normal&quot; gods tasked with ruling over the elementals? Personally, I find that idea boring and would rather just call them &quot;the god of fire&quot;, etc. Having them being created by Gaia? I guess, if I want them either less powerful, or just some form of &quot;super elementals&quot;.<br /> <br /> So it would put the exaltation of the dragon blooded in a direct line to Gaia. I can't see a problem with that. It would fit both the theme with &quot;a human can't hold the full exaltation of a primordial&quot; and &quot;terrestrial exalted are more powerful when they work together in a perfect circle.&quot;<br /> <br /> That actually gives me a few ideas on Gaia actually was behind and pulled the string leading up to the usurpation. Luna might have romanced Gaia just to trick her over to side with the Incarnae; even if that wasn't the case, doubt could have gnawed on Gaia (and perhaps fueled by the Yozis). UCS could have promised the control over Creation to Gaia, to be wielded through the 5ED, instead of having it stomped all over by the other primordials; but then seeing it being handed over to the Solars. Basically, UCS played her, and she is looking for payback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T02:12:10-07:00","id":173849,"title":"","content":"But the Law of Diminishment didn't effect the Incarnae, did it? So clearly it can be avoided if you're powerful enough, and the Dragons are on the same level as the Incarnae.<br /> I would be wary, especially in 3rd ed, where they want to get away from that kind of thing, of using blanket rules about how things work across the setting.<br /> With the bigger emphasis on mystery, I imagine that the nature of the Dragons is likely to be left mysterious in 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> Personally, I agree with Elfive. While I don't particularly think making the Dragons Gaia's souls makes them better, if they're not, well who is? Are there are a bunch of Gaian Devas wandering around Yu-Shan? Unless the devs have some good ideas for a few Gaian third-circle souls (which might liven up Yu-Shan a little), say they're the Dragons and call it a day. I understand the thing about not wanting to put everything into a slot, but I don't see why this particular thing is a massive sticking-point.<br /> <br /> Although, on the other hand, if they are her children... who's the daddy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can well imagine the Lunars funding heretic Immaculate cults who believe that the Dragons are also Luna's children, therefore they are subservient to Luna, and since the Dragons are the fundamental and transcendant parts of reality in Immaculate Doctrine, thus Luna essentially is the creator of the world and thus the greatest of Gods. Cue Pelleps Delled kicking people's skulls in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":".  Grammar 06-19-2014, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:53:35-07:00","id":174132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173815#post173815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exaltation -does- drain from it's Creator, as far as Third Edition is concerned. Exigence or no. It's the Law of Diminishment; when the Sun first made the Solar Exalted, he set for the first time. When Ten Sheaves used Exigence to Exalt Janest, he had to give up his life.<br /> How exactly this relates the the Elemental Dragons and their Chosen is uncertain, but I'd go ahead and suppose that it was the creation of the original bloodlines that Diminished the Dragons, rather than the Exaltation of individual Terrestrials.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Law of Diminishment is not confirmed to be a thing, In the same passage that mentions it, it also mentions it could be entirely made up. The only proof we have is of the Exigence taking away from Ten Sheaves to create Janest, but that is the Flame of Exigence, a different thing from Exaltations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:55:52-07:00","id":174134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173849#post173849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Law of Diminishment didn't effect the Incarnae, did it? So clearly it can be avoided if you're powerful enough, and the Dragons are on the same level as the Incarnae.<br /> I would be wary, especially in 3rd ed, where they want to get away from that kind of thing, of using blanket rules about how things work across the setting.<br /> With the bigger emphasis on mystery, I imagine that the nature of the Dragons is likely to be left mysterious in 3rd ed.<br /> <br /> Personally, I agree with Elfive. While I don't particularly think making the Dragons Gaia's souls makes them better, if they're not, well who is? Are there are a bunch of Gaian Devas wandering around Yu-Shan? Unless the devs have some good ideas for a few Gaian third-circle souls (which might liven up Yu-Shan a little), say they're the Dragons and call it a day. I understand the thing about not wanting to put everything into a slot, but I don't see why this particular thing is a massive sticking-point.<br /> <br /> Although, on the other hand, if they are her children... who's the daddy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can well imagine the Lunars funding heretic Immaculate cults who believe that the Dragons are also Luna's children, therefore they are subservient to Luna, and since the Dragons are the fundamental and transcendant parts of reality in Immaculate Doctrine, thus Luna essentially is the creator of the world and thus the greatest of Gods. Cue Pelleps Delled kicking people's skulls in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their father is Gaia, so is their mother. They're created wholesale by her, ergo they are her &quot;children&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:32:41-07:00","id":174161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173849#post173849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Law of Diminishment didn't effect the Incarnae, did it? So clearly it can be avoided if you're powerful enough, and the Dragons are on the same level as the Incarnae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this 'law' hasn't been really well described, and things can change, so it might not be canon, or may have a different form. But I have heard things about 'The first setting of the sun,' directly related to the Law of Diminishment, so it does seem to affect them. Now, Autochthon helped make the original Exalted, right? There was somewhere else I saw that suggested Autochthon's illness was related to that. So let's see:<br /> <br /> Solars: First setting of the sun, weakening him. (Incarnae)<br /> Autochthon: Creating the first Exalted weakened him greatly (Primordial)<br /> Yozis: Two of them tried to make Exalted, and it went badly... somehow. Could be the Law. (Yozis)<br /> I have not seen anything even remotely official regarding Lunars, Sidereals, Dragon-Blooded, Liminals, or Getimen yet. And of course Abyssal and Infernal shards weren't actually forged by Deathlords or Yozis, so probably aren't affected by the Law of Diminishment.<br /> <br /> Still, nothing published yet, so take it with a grain of salt. And maybe bake it with cheese, because that stuff is just fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:33:29-07:00","id":174162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=174134#post174134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their father is Gaia, so is their mother. They're created wholesale by her, ergo they are her &quot;children&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you say the same about literally any behemoth? What makes these guys special?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-19-2014, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:30:01-07:00","id":174199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173805#post173805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Ok, they're her children. woot. What does that even mean? What purpose does this distinction serve? ...</div> </div> </div> </div>To make it so that they're able to be something other than deva if that's what works for your game, more or less. They could be deva, yomi, gods, behemoths, unique beings, whatever. They are by the way that the word can be applied, more than the single thing laid down, as a goal of 3e is to make things broader, not to categorize the setting entirely into neat little boxes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173805#post173805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I mean, if you killed one that would damage creation, and in some ways Gaia is supposed to be or represent creation (because otherwise why is she even called Gaia?) and so effectively they'll act as if they were her souls even if they're not. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia isn't meant to be a representation of Creation. She's a Primordial who happens to ahve a real world earth titan name and at some point in <i>Exalted: the Autochtonians</i> and random parts of 2e she became tied to Creation in a way no other Primordial was due to this. I would go so far as to say divorcing the Five Elemental Dragons from her soul structure lets her be less a representation of Creation and so less hippy shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173805#post173805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... And Gaia has this big empty shelf where all her pantheon are supposed to go and I'm stood here watching everyone insist the 5ED go on their own fancy little table and I'm like &quot;for Christ's sake guys, they look fine on the shelf. Just put them there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This closes ideas, which existed in 1e. Making the dragons for sure her souls in effect closed an option, something that reinforcing them as her children opens back up. It also lets her shelf be acutally more diverse when it's not randomly taken up by five big dragons.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:37:18-07:00","id":174217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173776#post173776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Five Elemental Dragons are the children of Gaia, like the Incarnae are the children of Primordials. Gaia created them for a purpose and that was to serve as the anchors for Creation. They are not her souls, her souls are of and on Gnosis, beyond her jouten who remains in Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing on the term is it's supposed to be ambiguous. If you want them to be her souls, they are. If your ST decides they're gods, they're gods. The point is that it makes the 5ED less defined outright to open options. THem not being souls is a bit of consistency for me, so I prefer it. It lets all of Gaia be on Gnosis save her single jouten. And it divorces her from the mechanical processes of Creation like with other Primordials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173776#post173776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greater and Lesser Elemental Dragons are elementals who adopt the forms of dragons in respect and reverence of the Five. They are remnants of 5 great beings made by the Incarnae with the aid of Gaia and her children to tend Creation's elements. They were struck down, and scattered. Elementals of today are remnants and shards of that power. Like many spiritual beings, their forms are ultimately mutable. Some of their number are promoted to godhood, and given responsibilities of gods.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only the case in 2e. It is actually an outright retcon of previous stuff, where elementals didn't necessarily become dragons and dragons didn't seem to be elementals. Dragons were a confused thing in 1e in general, but I would go so far as to mix it up just because the elemental thing actually kind of bottlenecks elementals in a way.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:37:44-07:00","id":174220,"title":"","content":"Why does everyone insist on stuff being so fucking vague?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:43:35-07:00","id":174222,"title":"","content":"I prefer options to pin down in my games and things that give plot seeds rather than buying a world that's solved and that my PCs (or a pedant asshole like me) can toss at the ST. I would rather wordcount be used to open doors on potential plot seeds than exhaustively detail every bit.<br /> <br /> Having the dragons be obviously powerful beings who are now distant and hard to get to is interesting. Making what they are open means that I as an ST have more flexibility on defining what that is and what results occur if they get to them more than if they were just deva (which don't act a lot like deva).<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:55:32-07:00","id":174240,"title":"","content":"Off-the-wall idea: The EDs are actually <i>second</i> circle devas of Gaias fetitch: Creation itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:06:28-07:00","id":174253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173848#post173848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Referring to Gaia's 3rd circle parts as children instead of demons sounds like a good propaganda trick. &quot;Look. The Yozis are evil things. Gaia is nothing like them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is in part due to Primordials having soul hierarchies being something introduced after Gaia was introduced. The Dragons being her souls is something fanon glommed onto because it's what fit. When it became canon in 2e, it was the same edition that more or less said not Yozis, but <i>Primordials</i> have at least twelve souls. This is mechanically defined with Primordial Princiiple Emulation and the Pantheon Unfurling Charms, which defined things as fetch, + Willpower (10) + highest Virtue. Which is minimum twelve. Gaia is said to have five in <i>Roll of Glorious Divinity II</i> because the author pulled a standard 2e bit of not innovating and just working with the obvious material. This gets expanded to make her more the cosmic, diverse, and distant a bit in <i>Lands of Creation</i> (20 hidden souls) and Gnosis (<i>GotMH: Luna</i>).<br /> <br /> The dragons being her souls in a way stifled her. It made her feel weird as a Primordial as they were defined as alien multi-soul entities, it made her souls apparently rather samey due to them all being dragons, and it created other holes since apparently lesser and greater dragons aren't part of this and are only the bigger dragon's children in name, confusing where their Second Circle Deva would be.<br /> <br /> It's actually a matter of somewhat putting a square peg in a round hole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173848#post173848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... So there is a reference somewhere to Yozis having twelve 3rd circle parts? Well. Gaia isn't one of the defeated Primordials so she never had to swear the oats the Yosis had to swear. So having five parts as the Elemental Dragons, one &quot;jouten&quot; in Yu-Shan, and perhaps a couple more? Sounds like it would fit my view of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what is also defined. Insisting they're her souls, but then not using the souls in the way they are meant to (creating a cosmic monster corperation of mind entity) seems to me just checking off the numbers. The dragons feel kind of....dull as souls to be honest. Malfeas has a road, a dojo, an infinite manse and a sun as his souls. We see armies, moons, tides, entire cities, diseases, arenas, rivers, forests, ravines, arcangels, m usic players, and more as the sample Third Circle Demons we've seen. We've seen beings like the Core or potential deva like Viator.<br /> <br /> Gaia has elemental dragons. WHich is neat. But five of them. And oriignally, her only ones. And all they do is sleep. It just feels odd to me since it's a big space eaten up by them in her. The twenty hidden souls and Gnosis are kind of what made her more than a jouten with dragons attached because I feel that the dragons being her souls resulted in no one actually thinking she needed more. SHe hit the quota of &quot;multi-souled&quot; and folks moved on.<br /> <br /> Divorcing them from her in a way helps her be more her own being mythologically. It also allows the dragons to evolve storywise in ways not as impacted by Primordial wank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173848#post173848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ED being &quot;normal&quot; gods tasked with ruling over the elementals? Personally, I find that idea boring and would rather just call them &quot;the god of fire&quot;, etc. Having them being created by Gaia? I guess, if I want them either less powerful, or just some form of &quot;super elementals&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're apparently tied to the operation of Creation in a way. They are called &quot;the turning of the seasons&quot; in the same breath of the sun, moon, and stars. They can be gods of great power, but also gods of great weirdness. It works for the Maidens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173848#post173848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it would put the exaltation of the dragon blooded in a direct line to Gaia. I can't see a problem with that. It would fit both the theme with &quot;a human can't hold the full exaltation of a primordial&quot; and &quot;terrestrial exalted are more powerful when they work together in a perfect circle.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because general Primordial wankery is something I'm not a fan of, and the Dragon-Blooded should be recognized as drawing their power ultimately from badass fucking primeival dragons, not ultimately the &quot;real power of the Primordial&quot; shit that 2e liked a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=173848#post173848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That actually gives me a few ideas on Gaia actually was behind and pulled the string leading up to the usurpation. Luna might have romanced Gaia just to trick her over to side with the Incarnae; even if that wasn't the case, doubt could have gnawed on Gaia (and perhaps fueled by the Yozis). UCS could have promised the control over Creation to Gaia, to be wielded through the 5ED, instead of having it stomped all over by the other primordials; but then seeing it being handed over to the Solars. Basically, UCS played her, and she is looking for payback.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of exactly the opposite of where I gather 3e wants beings like her involved in the world, but that's abit of YCMV and your games are your own. The big thing, though, is that Gaia and the 5ED having a more ambiguous relationship opens options. Calling them her souls closes them.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:11:47-07:00","id":174258,"title":"","content":"Or maybe the 5ED are just <i>one</i> soul in five parts.<br /> <br /> Also fetitch + willpower+ highest virtue is the <i>maximum</i> number of souls. There's nothing to say that a primordial can't have less. And them all having a draconic form could be the same as most demons having a humanoid form. I'd be very surprised if they couldn't shapeshift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-19-2014, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:53:20-07:00","id":174402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=174258#post174258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe the 5ED are just <i>one</i> soul in five parts. Also fetitch + willpower+ highest virtue is the <i>maximum</i> number of souls. There's nothing to say that a primordial can't have less. And them all having a draconic form could be the same as most demons having a humanoid form. I'd be very surprised if they couldn't shapeshift.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beat me to the punch, I was going suggest that maybe they are all 5 her fetich, I wouldn't use that for all games, just where I would find it interesting. Something I miss from the older WW games is how they made everything an in character statement and there were several different ones with a disclosure of they could all be right or wrong, you would be given an idea with multiple possible answers. I apologize for the formatting, I'm posting from my phone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T12:13:17-07:00","id":174420,"title":"","content":"Another possibility is that they were originally just 5 third circle souls as different as any other, and not Gaia's only ones. When she selected them to stabilise creation she weaved their essence into the fabric of the world, along with their souls (hence no devas) and <i>then,</i> united by a common purpose, they decided to take on a common draconic theme.<br /> <br /> Maybe they and the original elementals are really one and the same, because if you actually read the description in the book it makes no sense whatsoever because it says that the elementals were created to maintain the flows of essence in creation, and then later on in the same paragraph mentions that the Elemental dragons were doing that anyway just by existing. <br /> <br /> Clearly someone somewhere got confused, and what <i>I</i> think happened (totally headcanon country here) was originally the 5ED worked just fine on their own, but the 3 spheres cataclysm destabilised creation to the point that the essence flows started leaking globs of power to put itself right that turned out to be sapient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T16:57:03-07:00","id":174698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=174220#post174220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does everyone insist on stuff being so fucking vague?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because vagueness is interesting. It kindles your imagination, makes you come up with your own answers, and this makes Creation different for every table, which brings it one step closer to it's mythic inspirations.<br /> <br /> Also, because if you want to feature the inner workings of the world as a plot point in your game, it's much more interesting when all the players don't know all the answers right off the bat. See also: people metagaming like mad for their characters to find out about the Great Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:13:01-07:00","id":174769,"title":"","content":"I just wish they went back to the way it was handled in the old WW games, give me what the different factions think the answers are and then put in a blurb about how they could all be wrong. that way the less creative have something to work with and the more experienced STs can just say, yeah, all that shit you read, it was wrong without the players having a conniption fit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:23:57-07:00","id":174790,"title":"","content":"back on topic though, the idea of the elementals turning into dragons seems pretty cool to me, creation doesn't have enough dragons and I also like the idea that they aren't gods, there are already to many god power players in the game lets have something else occupy the space<br /> <br /> and a good representation of a LED I think would be the stout earth dragon, something like the pics below<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.conceptart.org/forums/attachment.php?attachmentid=1392926\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://fc00.deviantart.net/fs21/f/2007/304/9/d/Dragon_of_earth_by_Ruth_Tay.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":359,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","user":"Dezeroth","date":". 06-19-2014, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:27:40-07:00","id":174942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=174134#post174134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their father is Gaia, so is their mother. They're created wholesale by her, ergo they are her &quot;children&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean it seriously (hence the smily). I meant it was the sort of thing poorly educated theologians might get into kung fu duels about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T00:31:51-07:00","id":175032,"title":"","content":"&quot;The dragons are said to be the Children of Gaia. Nobody is entirely sure what this means.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, actually several people are entirely sure what this means, but their answers don't match and inevitably fistfights ensue.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:26:37-07:00","id":175184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=174942#post174942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mean it seriously (hence the smily). I meant it was the sort of thing poorly educated theologians might get into kung fu duels about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that each of them was fathered by a different Primordial, who briefly courted Gaia andtried to keep her as a lover before she fell for Luna. That's five possible epic romance stories, right there. Possibilities just off the top of my head... Cytherea or Theion for fire, Metagaos or Szoreny for wood, Qaf or Mardukth for earth, Hegra for air (remember, Adorjan didn't exist yet), and Kimbery or Ta'azoka for water?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:43:20-07:00","id":175211,"title":"","content":"Are you trying to give the Immaculates an aneurysm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T08:42:04-07:00","id":175265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=175032#post175032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The dragons are said to be the Children of Gaia. Nobody is entirely sure what this means.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, actually several people are entirely sure what this means, but their answers don't match and inevitably fistfights ensue.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. One thing I do like about when the setting is vague, is when characters in the setting can discuss, argue, and fight over the answer to the great questions of life. If everything is answered, you just roll Lore. Boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T09:39:26-07:00","id":175311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=175211#post175211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you trying to give the Immaculates an aneurysm?</div> </div> </div> </div>What they don't know can't hurt them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:20:09-07:00","id":175354,"title":"","content":"Why the definition of 5ED have to be vague? Other things may be inaccurate: plans, relationships, history ... This works well with the Maidens.<br /> <br /> Would they be Incarnas because define them as souls of Gaia requires the construction of a number of other unnecessary souls. For this reason they were never built. If 5ED are Incarnas then it is easier to work with them. Serves its purpose being mysterious otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:31:52-07:00","id":175372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rochedo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=175354#post175354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would they be Incarnas because define them as souls of Gaia requires the construction of a number of other unnecessary souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. She's got X souls anyway, now she has X-5 souls plus the Dragons.<br /> I do see the point of those who've pointed out that it's weird she has 5 souls that are so similar though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:38:19-07:00","id":175375,"title":"","content":"My go-to explanation for getting rid of the second circles would to be that they were folded into creation when whatever the 5ED were before it was created were assigned to their positions. That's also why they follow a common theme. They didn't originally, but because they now had a united purpose they decided to get matching uniforms, as it were. <br /> <br /> I guess having them as the Incarnae of creation works too though. Or maybe call all five combined the Incarna of creation. Because I'm pretty sure The Maidens are technically <i>an </i>incarna as well, at least as far as some things are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T10:42:00-07:00","id":175377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/171852-lesser-elemental-dragons?p=175265#post175265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. One thing I do like about when the setting is vague, is when characters in the setting can discuss, argue, and fight over the answer to the great questions of life. If everything is answered, you just roll Lore. Boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Just let Lore represent truths, not facts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But as GM/ST/Whatyawannacallit I want to have a grasp of both the facts and the different truths (not that any of them has to be even close to what the writers had in mind). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T06:37:12-07:00","id":175965,"title":"","content":"another possible earth LED and just to mix it up a little bit a wood LED<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img3.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20120321051145/cartoonsandfiction/images/thumb/4/47/Earth_Dragon.jpg/300px-Earth_Dragon.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://37.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8ik2zjR0p1qg6k48o1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T09:36:41-07:00","id":176075,"title":"","content":"Ideals of adventures separated into five categories of elements. <br /> <b>Element air:</b> <br /> -The winds in the region are gone, the characters need to find out what happened to the Hurakas.<br /> -Confront a fanatical cult of a local god with the help of air elementals.<br /> <b>Element water:</b><br /> -Plague Cholera spreads in the region. Characters discover that there are many impurities in the wells and streams due to offense taken by the city against the water elementals.<br /> -Prevent a war between the raksha affect a city with the help of water elementals.<br /> <b>Element earth:</b><br /> -The floods are the leading edges of the rivers, the ground caved in various corners of the forest and the earth can not sustain crops. The characters need to restore the faith of Jokuns on your Gemlord.<br /> -Destroying a shadowlands with the help of earth elementals.<br /> <b>Element wood:</b><br /> -Various pests (grasshoppers, flies, aphids, frogs, weed and mold) happen at the same time making clear an ecological imbalance. The characters need to defend the Wood Spider in the region.<br /> -Hunting a free demon in Creation with the help of wood elementals.<br /> <b>Element fire:</b><br /> -Love marriage is taboo. Characters discover that an Ifrit questions the concept of family and love. Several clans came together to end this &quot;threat&quot;.<br /> -Save the escapees of a kingdom ravaged by fire and prevent the flames from spreading. with the help of fire elementals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T06:06:05-07:00","id":179614,"title":"","content":"Do Elementals follow the same age caps for essence that exalts do? Barring the ones actually born as dragons, I mean, because that's mentioned to be a thing that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}